course: dictionary
lesson: 4766
title: Houseplant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A houseplant is a plant that is grown in a pot indoors, inside a home, office or classroom. You can work out this meaning from the words around it, which are its context.
explain: «A houseplant should be watered when its soil feels dry, because too much water rots the roots.» The clues are watered, soil and dry. A houseplant is a plant in a pot that needs looking after, so it must be a plant that lives indoors.
explain: «A few houseplants do very little to clean the air of a room; opening a window does far more.» The sentence talks about a room, so a houseplant is one that sits inside it. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: it still makes sense.
fact: A houseplant is a plant grown in a pot indoors, in a home, office or classroom.
fact: «Houseplant» is a noun. The plural is houseplants.
fact: In science lessons, children study how houseplants need light, water and air. Some grow cress, spider plants or cacti on the windowsill.
fact: Some houseplants are poisonous, so keep them away from pets and small children, and never let anyone eat them.
fact: Too much water can rot the roots of a houseplant, so water it when its soil feels dry.
exercise: What is a houseplant? | A tree that grows in a forest | A weed that grows in a garden | A bush that grows by the sea | *A plant grown in a pot indoors, in a home, office or classroom
exercise: «A houseplant should be watered when its soil feels dry, because too much water rots the roots.» Why should you not give a houseplant too much water? | *It rots the roots | It makes the leaves grow too tall | It makes the soil too warm to see | It makes the pot too heavy to move
exercise: In «A few houseplants do very little to clean the air of a room», which word means more than one houseplant? | air | few | *houseplants | room
test: Which of these is a houseplant? | A rock on a beach | *A cactus grown in a pot on a windowsill | A fish in a pond | A bicycle kept in a shed
test: Why can some houseplants be a safety risk? | They are too heavy to lift | *They are poisonous if eaten by pets or small children | They make the room too dark | They need to be watered every hour
exam: What does «rots» mean in «too much water rots the roots»? | *Goes bad and decays | Dries out in the sun | Turns into soil | Grows bigger and taller
